comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T09:54:50.481Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-05: searched all statuses for Release tag checkout merge-driver bootstrap, exact-tag immutable publish recovery, and workflow_dispatch source selection. Closed pm-xvccnm owns the upstream Auto Release bootstrap; closed pm-t310hx owns already-published access recovery; open pm-ei6x66 owns the broader gate registry. None owns recovery of an existing but unpublished immutable tag plus downstream Release bootstrap. Source evidence: Auto Release run 30993783230 and Release run 30994468126."
  "2026-08-05T10:02:36.513Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the first direct focused run exposed two stale assertion strings after the recovery policy changed (61 passed, 2 failed). Corrected only those expectations, then added executable shell coverage for existing, missing, invalid-tag, and unexpected-registry source-selection outcomes. Focused rerun passes 64/64 across release workflow, automation, and runtime readiness contracts."
  "2026-08-05T10:14:16.783Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: linked PM test passes 64/64; typecheck and docs/skills pass; quality:static passes every SDK parity, token/context, tracker, registry, surface, and performance ratchet; full sandboxed coverage passes 433 files and 6,866 tests at exact 100% statements/branches/functions/lines; pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities; tracked secret scan is clean; packed npx smoke passes version 2026.8.5 with 15 packages; independent temporary-root package-first dogfood passes all 88 commands."
  "2026-08-05T10:14:48.114Z","harness:codex","Lifecycle correction: local implementation was closed too early even though acceptance explicitly requires hosted merge and production recovery. Reopened and reclaimed; this remains the sole active item until immutable tag, npm consumers, GitHub Release, and observability are proven."
  "2026-08-05T10:18:35.882Z","harness:codex","PR #902 opened at exact head 0c49710b354248f70edb4483254e689997f4e497. Sourcery reported weekly diff-character quota exhaustion; reacted and acknowledged as provider unavailability, not approval. Requested exact-head full reviews from CodeRabbit and Greptile with immutable-source and publication-boundary focus."
  "2026-08-05T10:22:04.109Z","harness:codex","Hosted CI evidence on PR #902 head 0c49710b: Gates (static) failed only at pm changelog freshness. Root cause was local clone missing newly created remote v2026.8.5 tag, while CI full-history checkout saw it. Fetched tags and verified local tag SHA equals origin SHA 0449d15f045f881a574248d35774a656a8b1e55b, then regenerated with published pm-changelog 2026.8.4; freshness check passes with the 2026.8.5 dated boundary."
  "2026-08-05T10:39:16.151Z","harness:codex","Production recovery run 30997619576 selected exact tag source and passed build, clone bootstrap, typecheck, docs, and full coverage, then failed tracker measurement only: historical tag tracker observed 204 validate-files-missing-linked-paths vs open owner pm-j8z6 ceiling 195. Merge-driver violations are fixed. Remediation must not close/raise pm-j8z6 or alter the immutable tag: gate tagged code against reviewed current-main PM context, then restore and prove the exact tagged tree before artifact generation/publication."
  "2026-08-05T10:52:37.535Z","harness:codex","Root-cause refinement from exact path diff: all nine extra missing paths were .agents/pm/extensions/pm-changelog and its tracked package files. A developer checkout already has the managed extension installed, but a clean tagged checkout reaches quality:static before changelog:pm:check installs it. Reordered changelog verification/install before static measurement; a fresh detached v2026.8.5 worktree now reports tracker ratchet passed (19 enforced, 0 retired, 2,318 items) and gate registry passed (12 registered, 46 enforced, 3 claims)."
  "2026-08-05T11:14:13.071Z","harness:codex","Production evidence: exact-tag recovery run 30999751366 passed full coverage, pm-changelog clean-checkout install, static tracker/gate registry, context, compatibility, packaging, npx tarball, and package-first dogfood, then failed at npm publication. The workflow unconditionally attempted npm access set before anonymous probes; the automation token correctly cannot perform account-level access mutation (E403), while an anonymous fresh-cache npm view confirms @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.4 is already public. Fix is to honor the documented guard order: exact-version probe, main-source refusal, package visibility probe and publish; access recovery only when neither target nor package is anonymously visible."
  "2026-08-05T11:18:06.776Z","harness:codex","TDD remediation evidence: executable publication-guard tests now model workflow_dispatch with an anonymously visible target and with a public package plus missing target; both prove no npm access mutation occurs, while hidden-package E404/E403 recovery controls remain covered. Linked suite passes 64/64. Typecheck, docs/skills, pnpm audit (no known vulnerabilities), tracked secret scan, and generated changelog check pass."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T10:14:17.275Z","harness:codex","Release recovery design: workflow_dispatch begins on reviewed main. An authenticated exact-version probe selects main only for an existing immutable npm version; a definitive missing-version result resolves and detaches the requested tag; every other registry failure stops. Only tagged source may publish a missing version. The built tagged CLI installs clone-local merge-driver configuration before tracker-bearing static gates."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T10:14:17.718Z","harness:codex",A downstream tag workflow has independent clone-local state even when its upstream auto-release job installed merge drivers. Recovery of an unpublished immutable version must execute the current reviewed workflow definition while pinning build and publication inputs to the existing tag commit; re-running the historical workflow alone cannot acquire the workflow fix.
  "2026-08-05T10:52:38.264Z","harness:codex",Clean-checkout tracker measurements must install declared managed extensions before linked-file validation. Local developer workspaces can mask this ordering dependency because extension trees persist outside committed source; compare exact missing-path sets in a fresh worktree before attributing a ratchet increase to historical tracker debt.
  "2026-08-05T11:18:07.333Z","harness:codex",Publish-capable npm automation credentials can legitimately be forbidden from package access mutations. Registry recovery must establish anonymous target/package visibility first and reserve npm access changes for the genuinely hidden-package ambiguity; otherwise a healthy public package is blocked before immutable publication.
